  "query_preview": "..\nOverall dry conditions have moved into most of the Marianas this \nafternoon, with Guam seeing a few island effect showers linger \nduring the mid-afternoon hours. Tinian and Saipan look to remain \nfairly dry over the next several days, and into next week. However, \nwith the light winds expected through Tuesday, Saipan has a risk of \nisland convection for the next few days. So POPs (Probability of \nPrecipitation) were increased to 30 percent for the afternoons at \nSaipan. For Guam, expect increased showers and isolated thunderstorms\nto move into the area later tonight, near midnight, as the monsoon \ntrough drifts northwest with TS Surigae. This will maintain low-end \nscattered showers and isolated thunderstorms for Guam through Friday \nnight. For Saturday through Tuesday, light and variable winds will \nalso maintain the risk of island convection through Tuesday. \nOtherwise, a drier pattern is expected for the remainder of the \nforecast.",
